    description: "FOUND 2026-09-03 while measuring before filing the Java registry gap (owner\nasked whether a tracker item existed). Tree: dev 68db7bd6e5. Rig:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/javareg_09032026/ (README first).\n\nTHE SHAPE. java.py's receiver typing (var_types) has four sources, and its own\n_ParsedFile docstring lists exactly four: (1) `new T()` initializers, (2) the\nreturn type of a RESOLVED in-repo method whose return type is an in-repo class,\n(3) parameter declarations, (4) field declarations. The DECLARED TYPE OF A LOCAL\nVARIABLE is not among them. Measured, one fixture per shape, dst read off the\nemitted edge:\n\n    FileWriter w = new FileWriter(p); w.write(..)       java.io.FileWriter.write   typed\n    var w = makeWriter(); w.write(..)   (same file)     java.io.FileWriter.write   typed (source 2)\n    OutputStream o = null; o.write(1)                    java:external:0-0:o.write  UNTYPED\n    OutputStream o = this.field; o.write(2)              java:external:0-0:o.write  UNTYPED\n    OutputStream o = sock.getOutputStream(); o.write(3)  java:external:0-0:o.write  UNTYPED\n    Connection c = DriverManager.getConnection(u); c.close()  java:external:0-0:c.close  UNTYPED\n    OutputStream o; o = sock.getOutputStream(); o.write(4)    java:external:0-0:o.write  UNTYPED\n    catch (IOException e) { e.getMessage() }             untyped (catch_formal_parameter is not read)\n    for (User u : users) { u.getName() }                 untyped (enhanced_for_statement is not read)\n\nThe two sites that DO type a local both read the INITIALIZER (java.py ~2311:\nobject_creation_expression under a variable_declarator; ~1977: a resolved\nmethod's return type, gated on `ret_name in class_symbols`) and never the\ndeclaration's `type` field. Parameters and fields ARE read from their declared\ntypes (1732, 1744), so the local declaration is the one omission. The receiver\nthen falls to the untyped-external path, which glues the receiver NAME into\nthe callee (`o.write`) -- WI-nakut's \"java carries the receiver in the name\".\n\nSIZE, guacamole-client (849 files, tree-sitter count of the binding shapes;\nshapes_guac.py):\n\n    1,210  T x = <method_invocation>      never typed\n      358  catch (T e)                    never typed\n      163  for (T x : xs)                 never typed\n       89  T x;  (assigned later)         never typed\n       34  T x = (T) expr                 never typed\n       17  T x = null                     never typed\n      315  T x = new T(..)                typed today\n        0  var x = ...                    (guacamole does not use `var`)\n\nand on the emitted graph: 3,136 of 9,174 calls edges (34.2%) carry an untyped\nreceiver; the top receiver names are `e` (148), `model`, `parser`, `object`,\n`user`, `entry`, `connection`. Java DECLARES its types; the analyzer types 315\nbindings out of ~2,180 and reads the declaration for none of them.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS. INV-linub's exposure table: 67 of java's 69 sinks (97%) are\nmethod-kind rows that need a typed receiver before the F3 gate will admit them.\nWI-nasuf's fixture reported java as \"emits + matches\" in both forms -- true, and\nonly because that fixture constructed its receivers inline (`new File(p)`).\nEvery `Connection c = DriverManager.getConnection(..)`, every\n`OutputStream o = socket.getOutputStream()`, every `BufferedReader r =\nFiles.newBufferedReader(p)` is invisible to java.yaml today. NOT WI-lalot:\nthat item supplies return types for LIBRARY producers, which Java needs only\nfor `var` and for chains; a declaration is stronger evidence than any\ninference and is already in the source.\n\nFIX SHAPE. In the var_types pre-pass, read `local_variable_declaration.type`\n(when it is not `var`), `catch_formal_parameter`'s type, and\n`enhanced_for_statement`'s type, qualified through the file's imports the way\nparameters already are; a declaration wins over an initializer inference when\nboth exist (they cannot disagree in valid Java except through subtyping, where\nthe declared type is the one the catalogue rows are written against). Then the\nINV-linub rule: measure through L4 ON FINDINGS on guacamole-client, not on\nedges, and read every newly typed row back (a typed receiver newly matching a\nmethod-kind sink is the F3 gate's exact false-positive class if the type is\nwrong). Sweep the other JVM analyzers (kotlin, scala inherit java.yaml) by\nfixture, not by reading -- kotlin's L2 gate (WI-nasuf) means its row may not\neven emit."  # 6544
    fields:  # 6544
      statement: "A catalogued I/O call on a receiver whose type the source DECLARES (T x = ..., catch (T e), for (T x : xs)) carries that type into the module slot regardless of the initializer's shape (INV-linub L3 for Java)."  # 6544
      root_cause: "java.py's var_types pre-pass types a local only from its INITIALIZER (new T() at ~2311; a resolved in-repo method's return type at ~1977) and never reads local_variable_declaration.type, catch_formal_parameter or enhanced_for_statement; parameters and fields are read from their declarations, locals are not."  # 6544
