  nonce: '90e3'  # 90e3
  message: "FIXED IN PR #750 (dev 7f6c0493b0). Root cause as filed, plus three defects the\nread-back found in the fix itself before it shipped.\n\nWHAT LANDED. `_extract_edges` binds the DECLARED type of a local\n(`local_variable_declaration` with a non-`var` type), a single-type catch\nparameter, a for-each variable, a try-with-resources `resource`, an\nexplicitly typed lambda parameter, a record's components, a generic or\ninline-qualified field (`Map<String, String> attrs` -- only a bare\ntype_identifier field child was read before), and a field declared in an\nANCESTOR class, qualified through the parent's own file imports\n(`_inherited_field_module`; a project-class field type is left to the\nTier-2 linker's Site-3 walk exactly as before). Precedence: declaration first (pre-order), a\n`new T()` initializer NARROWS it (the object IS that class; pinned by\n`test_constructor_initialiser_still_narrows_the_declared_type`), and a\nreturn-type INFERENCE never overrides a declaration -- measured reason below.\nLocals are scoped to their method by a scope stack keyed on the method's end\nbyte; fields and parameters keep the file-wide binding they had.\n\nThe module slot for a declared type: the import, an inline `java.sql.Connection`,\na nested `Map.Entry` on an imported outer, the wildcard-package disjunction, or\n`java.lang.<T>` for the CLOSED list `_JAVA_LANG_TYPES` only -- a forgotten\n`import java.io.InputStream` must not become `java.lang.InputStream` (the\npresent-but-wrong hint INV-kotob calls worse than untyped). A type parameter\n`<T>` is excluded; a project class stays a `receiver_type_hint` for the Tier-2\nlinker and never enters the slot.\n\nMEASURED THROUGH L4 ON FINDINGS, guacamole-client (the item's own rig):\nio-boundaries 38 -> 40 chains, +2, 0 lost -- `FileInputStream keyStreamIn = null`\n(declared, assigned later) reaching `FileInputStream.read`, and `Path\nextensionTempLibDir = null` reaching `Path.toFile`; both read back against\nsource. Small because guacamole's declared locals are mostly uncatalogued types\n(String, List, Map, Matcher, its own classes); the L2/L3 movement is where the\nvolume is.\n\nREAD BACK PER CALL SITE, both arms in one process (rig in\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/vugon_javadecl_09032026/, README first):\n  guacamole-client  9,105 sites: 1,662 untyped -> typed, 257 -> project hint,\n                    190 hint -> typed, 0 sites lost a type, 36 re-keys.\n  keycloak          386,340 sites: 67,400 untyped -> typed, 12,419 -> project\n                    hint, 3,906 hint -> typed, 166 lost a type, 1,765 re-keys.\nThe 166: 80 are bare lambda parameters (`kcGroup -> kcGroup.getId()`),\nthe rest `var` bound to a call the resolver cannot see (a nested class's\nstatic factory, an inherited method) or a project-class field inherited\nfrom a parent (handed to the linker's Site-3 walk, unchanged). Every one is\na type the old arm had only by LEAK from a sibling method -- and three were\nWRONG (`FirefoxOptions` on an HtmlUnit receiver, `ProviderConfigurationBuilder`\non a Quarkus one, `Future` on a String). The 1,765 re-keys collapse to 429\ntype pairs; the twelve largest were read against source (`List<String> args`\nfor a leaked `String`, `Map attributes` for a leaked `Attributes`, a typed\nlambda `(OIDCClientRepresentation clientRep) ->` for a leaked\n`ClientRepresentation`, `Validator validator = Validators.integerValidator()`\nwhere the old arm carried the in-repo inference) and every one is the\ndeclaration in scope.\nEVERY re-key on guacamole was read: all 36 are the OLD arm carrying a type\nleaked from another method's parameter (`user.setPassword` typed\n`ActivityRecord`, `identifiers.add` typed `Collection` for a declared `Set`)\nand the new arm carrying the declaration in scope.\n\nTHREE DEFECTS THE READ-BACK FOUND IN THE FIX (LIVE.md rule 8), each fixed and\npinned before the PR:\n 1. An anonymous class body inside a method carries a `method_declaration`;\n    \"restore locals when the next method begins\" closed the ENCLOSING scope,\n    unbinding `protocol_directory` for the `getAbsolutePath()` after it. ->\n    scope stack.\n 2. `String ksmConfig = group.getAttributes().get(k); ksmConfig.trim()` was\n    retyped `Future`: the chained `.get` has no receiver name, the\n    current-class lookup resolved it to an anonymous Supplier's `get()`, and\n    the return-type arm overrode the declaration. `Connectable connectable =\n    type.getConnectable()` likewise became `Connection` through an\n    enum-constant covariant override (name-keyed registry, first wins). ->\n    inference never overrides a declaration.\n 3. keycloak declares every LDAPQuery / RandomAccessFile in try-with-resources\n    (`resource`, not `local_variable_declaration`) -- 331 sites the old arm\n    had typed only by leak went untyped. -> `resource` binds. The same pass\n    found record components (`record Connector(CountDownLatch latch, ..)`)\n    and ancestor-declared fields (`protected RealmModel realm` in\n    AbstractTokenExchangeProvider, used by every subclass) typed only by\n    leak -> both bind.\n\nSTILL OPEN, filed rather than chased: a bare lambda parameter (`s -> s.trim()`)\nstays untyped; typing it from the declared functional-interface type argument\n(`Function<SdJwt, ...> f = sdJwt -> ...`) is a separate inference. Block-level\nscoping is method-level: two sequential `for (A x : ..)` / `for (B x : ..)`\nloops rebind correctly, but a for-each variable shadowing a FIELD of the same\nname keeps the loop type for the rest of the method.\n\nkotlin / scala (inherit java.yaml) NOT swept here -- kotlin's L2 gate\n(WI-nasuf) means its row may not emit at all; that is the next PR in this\nqueue."  # 90e3
